{"content":"q20. **Server-Sent Events (SSE)**; **server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go**; **CreateMemo, UpdateMemo, DeleteMemo, CreateMemoComment, UpsertMemoReaction, DeleteMemoReaction**\n\n**Mechanism**: Server-Sent Events (SSE) over HTTP with `Content-Type: text/event-stream`. The handler at `server/router/api/v1/sse_handler.go:32-34` (`handleSSE`) manages the `/api/v1/sse` endpoint, which clients connect to via Bearer token authentication. The connection stays open while the server pushes events.\n\n**Hub Implementation**: `SSEHub` type at `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go:56-60` manages concurrent client subscriptions (line 56). It maintains a map of active `SSEClient` connections (line 58) and provides `Broadcast()` (line 115) to send events to all eligible clients based on visibility filtering (private events only to creator or admin, public/protected to all).\n\n**Memo Handlers Broadcasting Through Hub**:\n1. `CreateMemo` (memo_service.go:70) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCreated` at line 163\n2. `UpdateMemo` (memo_service.go:401) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoUpdated` via `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` helper at memo_update_helpers.go:71\n3. `DeleteMemo` (memo_service.go:518) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoDeleted` at line 585\n4. `CreateMemoComment` (memo_service_comments.go:20) — broadcasts `SSEEventMemoCommentCreated` at line 126\n5. `UpsertMemoReaction` (reaction_service.go:60) — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionUpserted` at line 106\n6. `DeleteMemoReaction` (reaction_service.go:111) — broadcasts `SSEEventReactionDeleted` at line 161","iteration":8,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
